# How much to accept: an adaptive concurrency limit (Netflix concurrency-limits README; Envoy adaptive concurrency filter docs, latest Oct 2026).
...@_style
direction: down
static: "fixed RPS limit\nstress-test the tipping point, set it below\n(say 75%, Netflix's example), token bucket\nautoscaling makes it go stale" {class: ext}
law: "Little's Law\nrequests in flight = RPS x average latency" {class: svc}
meas: "measure latency\nvs a baseline\n(Vegas: minRTT · Gradient2: long-window average)" {class: focus}
down: "latency above baseline\nqueue forming: lower the limit" {class: warn}
up: "latency near baseline\nraise the limit" {class: ok}
rej: "past the limit: reject fast\nclear 'overloaded' signal + back-off hint\nnot a timeout, not an invitation to retry" {class: bad}
static -> law: "replace with"
law -> meas
meas -> down
meas -> up
down -> meas {style.stroke-dash: 4}
up -> meas {style.stroke-dash: 4}
down -> rej
envoy: "Envoy adaptive concurrency filter\ngradient = (minRTT + B) / sampleRTT\nlimit_new = gradient x limit_old + headroom" {class: note}
google: "Google SRE book ch. 21: reject when active threads\n(smoothed) grow beyond the number of CPUs" {class: note}
